    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/psac-ra-ii-history-researcher-and-indexing-assistant/": {
      "title": "PSAC – RA II – Researcher and Indexing Assistant – History",
      "description": "PSAC – RA II – Researcher and Indexing Assistant – History | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities PSAC – RA II – Researcher and Indexing Assistant… PSAC – RA II – Researcher and Indexing Assistant – History Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on Friday, October 23, 2026. Classification: Research Assistant II Employee Group : PSAC Job Title: Researcher and Indexing Assistant Department : History, Faculty of Arts Wage or Salary : $18.73/hr Number of Hours to Work : 48 Start Date : October 30, 2026 Number of Positions available : 1 End Date of Employment: April 30, 2027 Course title and number (if applicable): NA Date Issued : Wednesday, October 14, 2026 Qualifications/Experience: Completion of 3rd year of university studies. Ability to work in digital archives; affinity with microfiche and digital documents. Ability to manage large data files, and decode abbreviations and coded information. The ability to work with extreme precision: high attention to details as indexing of diaries and log books has to be done with absolute precision. Accountability: the ability to reach out and ask for assistance if problems in the indexing process arise. Keeping a log of activities and completed hours of work, and ability to navigate and entering the hours into the payroll Key Duties: The Research Assistant will provide support to Dr. Harms and the Anisinew Okimawin Tribal Council of Island lake on a project of historical recovery. Duties entail indexing of an extensive volume digitized materials that were transcribed in a previous phase of the research, to allow for their thematic organization, and facilitate coding and analysis. To Apply: Send a Cover Letter and CV to Dr. Patricia Harms at harmsp@brandonu.ca Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
