    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/psac-ra-ii-transcriber-sociology/": {
      "title": "PSAC",
      "description": "PSAC – RA II – Transcriber – Sociology | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities PSAC – RA II – Transcriber – Sociology PSAC – RA II – Transcriber – Sociology Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on Friday, October 23, 2026. Classification: Research Assistant II Employee Group : PSAC Job Title: Transcriber Department : Sociology, Faculty of Arts Wage or Salary : $18.73/hr Number of Hours to Work : 48 Start Date : October 30, 2026 Number of Positions available : 1 End Date of Employment: April 30, 2027 Course title and number (if applicable): NA Date Issued : Wednesday, October 14, 2026 Qualifications/Experience: Completion of 3rd year of university studies. Ability to read CURSIVE and the ability to decode abbreviations and codified information. Affinity with microfiche and digital documents. The ability to work with extreme precision: high attention to details as the language of the log books must be reproduced with absolute precision . Accountability: the ability to reach out and ask for assistance if problems in the translation arise. Keeping a log of activities and completed hours of work, and ability to navigate and entering the hours into the payroll platform “Workforce” Ability to self-manage and work independently. Key Duties: The Research Assistant will provide support to Dr. Petrella and the Anisinew Okimawin Tribal Council of Island lake on a project of historical recovery. The duties entail the transcription of cursive log books into digitized files, using the program Excel. To Apply: Email a cover letter and CV to Dr. Serena Petrella, at petrellas@brandonu.ca. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/2026-executive-assistant-finance-and-registration-full-time-regular/": {
      "title": "2026 – Executive Assistant, Finance and Registration, Full-time, Regular",
      "description": "2026 – Executive Assistant, Finance and Registration, Full-time, Regular | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities 2026 – Executive Assistant, Finance and Registration, … 2026 – Executive Assistant, Finance and Registration, Full-time, Regular Duties and Responsibilities The Executive Assistant to the Vice-President (Administration & Finance) (VP A&F) provides high-level, confidential administrative support and serves as a liaison between the VP’s office and internal and external stakeholders. The Executive Assistant is responsible for coordinating the schedule of the VP (A&F), arranging meetings and appointments, preparing relevant meeting materials, maintaining confidential files, responding to general inquiries, and managing contact listings. The role provides administrative support through the preparation of committee materials, organization of meeting facilities, coordination of catering services, editing and distribution of meeting minutes, assistance with reports and presentations, and maintenance of the office website. This position also supports compliance-related functions such as FIPPA requests, assisting with data collection, redacting information as directed, and preparing correspondence. General office duties are required, along with providing administrative support on key committees and other duties as assigned. Qualifications To be considered for this role, candidates must possess a one-year certificate in Office Administration or a similar program, along with a minimum of three years’ experience in a comparable position. A combination of relevant education and experience may also be considered. Experience within a post-secondary institution, the public sector, or a unionized environment is considered an asset. The ability to exercise discretion when accessing or handling confidential information is vital. Candidates must demonstrate strong interpersonal, organizational, and time management skills, and be able to work collaboratively with both internal and external stakeholders. Proficiency in office software is critical, and success in this role requires a high level of professionalism, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple tasks efficiently. Salary : Excluded Support Staff III (ESS – III) position with a salary of $64,584.00 per annum. What to Submit If your qualifications, skills and work experience align with this position, we welcome you to apply by submitting one PDF file that includes your resume, cover letter, and citizenship status with the subject line: 2026 – Executive Assistant, Administration & Finance by 4:30 p.m . on October 23, 2026 to: hrapplications@brandonu.ca Please Note: This position is subject to a Criminal Record Check and Child Abuse Registry Check and the successful candidate will be responsible for fees incurred. Candidates may be required to successfully complete a technical skills test. We thank all applicants for their interest in this position, however, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. Should you require an accommodation during any phase of the recruitment process, contact HR at hr@brandonu.ca . All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/research-assistant-iii-department-of-psychology-9/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant III",
      "description": "Research Assistant III – Department of Psychology | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Research Assistant III – Department of Psychology Research Assistant III – Department of Psychology Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on October 29, 2026 Classification: Research Assistant III Employee Group : PSAC Job Title: Research Assistant Department : Psychology Wage or Salary : $22.01/hr Number of Hours to Work : 300 Start Date : November 2, 2026 Number of Positions available : 2 End Date of Employment: until March 31, 2027 Course title and number (if applicable): NA Date Issued : October 23, 2026 Qualifications/Experience: This project is part of a larger SSHRC-funded project on Age-Friendly Communities in Manitoba. Duties for this position will include helping to organize and run focus groups with primarily French-speaking adults aged 50+ living in Manitoba. Duties will also include liaising with MB organizations and transcription. Duties may also include research on topics relating to social connection in French Canadians. Tasks will also include other relevant duties, as assigned. Qualifications/Experience: Ability to work well independently with minimal supervision and have excellent organizational skills. Strong abilities in communication (in English and French). Ideal candidates will be upper-level undergraduates (4th yr +). Ideally, the candidate will have skills in conducting research, including focus groups or evaluation, knowledge and understanding of gerontology (study of older adulthood), knowledge/experience in working with older adults. Completion of TCPS-2: CORE ethics. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, TCPS-2: CORE certificate, and names of two references to Dr. Nancy Newall, newalln@brandonu.ca. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/student-assistant-ii-indigenous-peoples-centre/": {
      "title": "Student Assistant II",
      "description": "Student Assistant II – Indigenous Peoples’ Centre | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Student Assistant II – Indigenous Peoples’ Centr… Student Assistant II – Indigenous Peoples’ Centre Classification: Student Assistant II Employee group: PSAC Job title: IPC Elder & Student Hub Assistant Department: Indigenous Peoples’ Centre Wage: $17.94/hour (SA II or Research Assistant I) Hours of work: 3 hours per week per position Start date: November 2, 2026 Number of Positions: 4 Length of appointment: November 2, 2026 to April 30, 2027 Date issued: October 23, 2026 Application deadline: October 29, 2026 by 4:30 p.m. Duties: 1. Greet and welcome people entering the Indigenous Peoples’ Centre 2. Assist the IPC staff and faculty host events 3. Provide assistance with accessing Indigenous Peoples’ Centre resources 4. Help to keep the IPC spaces organized, tidy and stocked 5. Other relevant duties as assigned 6. Work with minimal supervision 7. Working hours may include day, evening or weekend shifts, as needed Qualifications/Experience: 1. Limited advanced skills and judgment 2. Ability to work independently and/or with others effectively 3. Ability to work courteously with fellow students, faculty, and staff 4. Ability to communicate clearly and effectively 5. Detail-oriented, punctual and reliable 6. Experience as a student leader will be considered an asset Education: 1. Preference given to a current Indigenous Brandon University student 2. Good academic standing To Apply: Send resume to: DuBoisA@BrandonU.ca Alison DuBois, A/Director, Indigenous Peoples Centre Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. Should you require an accommodation during any phase of the recruitment process, contact HR at hr@brandonu.ca . All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
