      "description": "Research Assistant III for the International Students’ Experiences, Motivation, Engagement, and Belonging Study | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Research Assistant III for the International Students’… Research Assistant III for the International Students’ Experiences, Motivation, Engagement, and Belonging Study Position Vacancy Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on November 5, 2026 Classification: Research Assistant III Employee Group: PSAC Job Title: Research Assistant III for the International Students’ Experiences, Motivation, Engagement, and Belonging Study Department: CREAMS Research Lab (Culture & Regulation of Learning for Engagement, Academic Motivation, and Success) Wage or Salary: $22.01/hr SAIV OR RAIII Number of Hours to Work: 200 hours total, with flexible scheduling based on research activities and project needs. Start Date: November 9, 2026 Number of Positions available: 1 End Date of Employment: June 30, 2027 Course title and number (if applicable): N/A Date Issued: Oct. 28, 2026 Qualifications/Experience: Enrollment in, or completion of, an undergraduate or graduate degree in Education, Psychology, Sociology, Social Work, International/Global Studies, Anthropology, or a related discipline. Previous experience assisting with academic research, particularly surveys, interviews, participant recruitment, qualitative coding, and quantitative data analysis. Knowledge of international students’ experiences in Canadian higher education, including challenges and opportunities relating to academic adjustment, belonging, institutional support, motivation, and engagement. Experience as an international student or demonstrated engagement with international student communities. Familiarity with culturally responsive teaching, self-regulated learning, educational psychology, student motivation, and engagement. Experience working with culturally diverse student populations, including African, Black, and Caribbean student communities. Familiarity with qualitative or/and quantitative analysis software such as NVivo, ATLAS.ti, SPSS, or R. Experience conducting literature reviews and preparing academic research reports. Key Duties: Recruitment of participants, data collection (i.e., survey, interviews and focused groups). Conduct literature reviews Qualitative (e.g., thematic) and quantitative (e.g., correlation, regression, exploratory factor) data analyses. Assist in examining culturally responsive teaching and self-regulated learning practices, including analyzing lesson plans and instructional materials in relation to the study’s conceptual framework. Support the planning, coordination, and documentation of teacher learning team meetings, professional development activities, classroom implementation, and observations. Conduct literature review and prepare summaries relating to culturally responsive teaching, self-regulated learning, student motivation, engagement, belonging, and institutional support. Be able to work independently and collaboratively with other RAs, and participate in relevant hybrid or/and online CREAMS research lab/project meetings. Perform other related assigned duties. To Apply: Send your cover letter, CV with names of two references, and TCPS-2: CORE certificate all in one PDF to Dr. Aloy Anyichie, anyichiea@brandonu.ca Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. 10.2026 Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
