ith the Culturally Responsive Self-Regulated Learning (CR-SRL) Framework. Experience conducting literature searches, organizing data, or preparing academic summaries. Familiarity with qualitative or quantitative research methods. Interest in working with high school research, teachers, or educational institutions. Willingness to develop skills in qualitative coding, survey data analysis, and research software. The appointment may be extended to June 30, 2027, or additional hours authorized, subject to available funding, and satisfactory performance. Key Duties: Assist with participant recruitment, survey administration, interview scheduling, and organization of research materials. Transcribe interviews, organize and clean survey data, and maintain accurate research records. Support preliminary coding and analysis of interview transcripts, lesson plans, and other instructional materials. Conduct literature searches and prepare summaries on culturally responsive teaching, self-regulated learning, motivation, and engagement. Assist with teacher learning team activities, classroom implementation documentation, and research reporting. Participate in research team meetings and relevant CREAMS Research Lab activities, while maintaining research ethics and confidentiality. Be able to work independently and collaboratively with other RAs, and participate in relevant CREAMS research lab/project meetings. Perform other related assigned duties. To Apply: Send your cover letter, CV with names of two references, and TCPS-2: CORE certificate all in one PDF to Dr. Aloy Anyichie, anyichiea@brandonu.ca Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. 10.2026 Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
