    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/student-assistant-iv-group-tutor-sociology-2/": {
      "title": "Student Assistant IV",
      "description": "Student Assistant IV – Group Tutor-Sociology | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Student Assistant IV – Group Tutor-Sociology Student Assistant IV – Group Tutor-Sociology Classification: Student Assistant IV Employee group: PSAC Job title: Group Tutor – Sociology Department: Indigenous Peoples’ Centre Wage: $22.01/hour (SA IV or Research Assistant III) Hours of work: 5 hours per week Start date: November 16, 2026 Number of Positions: 1 Length of appointment: November 16, 2026 to April 26, 2027 Date issued: October 28, 2026 Application deadline: November 6, 2026 by 4:30 p.m. Duties: Assist students with developing an understanding of course work. Explain concepts, clarify information, answer student questions, and offer support. Help students prepare for tests/exams and assignments. Model student success strategies. and other relevant duties as assigned. Qualifications/Experience: Current Brandon University student – Students majoring in Sociology (3rd year or above) preferred – Strong communication skills and ability to work one-on-one or with a group – Ability to help students develop their problem-solving skills with enthusiasm – Demonstrated patience and ability to relate to students with varying learning styles – Ability to work independently with little or no supervision – Previous experience as a group tutor within the Indigenous Peoples’ Centre is an   asset To Apply: Please submit cover letter, resume and contact information for 3 referencest to: Suelee Innes, Indigenous Student Transition Program Coordinator Email: InnesS@BrandonU.ca Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, person