    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/2026-labour-relations-specialist/": {
      "title": "2026 – Labour Relations Specialist",
      "description": "2026 – Labour Relations Specialist | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities 2026 – Labour Relations Specialist 2026 – Labour Relations Specialist Applications are invited for a Labour Relation Specialist to join our Human Resources team.  We are looking for an experienced Human Resources professional with experience working within unionized environments to help foster and maintain collegial labour relations. This role is responsible for collective bargaining, labour relations administration, and records management. Duties and Responsibilities Under the supervision of the Associate Vice-President, People and Talent, the Labour Relations Specialist provides guidance and interpretation of the various Collective Agreements; addresses day-to-day matters related to CA understanding for five (5) Collective Agreements; participates in labour management meetings, creates Letters of Understanding/Memorandums of Agreement, represents the University in grievance hearings, drafts response letters; schedules, coordinates, attends pre-bargaining meetings with stakeholders to understand issues related to existing CAs, drafts proposals, presents and negotiates as the Management Spokesperson at negotiations;  updates existing CAs with agreed language, implements revisions, and conducts training sessions for stakeholders. Qualifications To be considered, candidates must have an undergraduate degree with a focus in Human Resources along with additional training in Labour Relations, with a minimum of five (5) years related experience in labour relations; an equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered.  CPHR designation is highly preferred. Candidates must have experience with all aspects of collective bargaining.  Experience working with multiple bargaining units within one organization is key to being successful in this role. Previous employment in public sector or post-secondary education is a desirable asset. The successful candidate has a strong ability to be proactive and take initiative when addressing issues for resolution, use sound judgment, be prepared to have difficult conversations with stakeholders, possess a thorough understanding of legislation, Collective Agreements, and regulations applicable to University employees. Maintaining confidentiality, making decisions under pressure, and working collaboratively across a wide range of stakeholders are necessary skills the successful candidate must possess. Salary: Managers & Professional Officers MPO-VI  $104,716.00 What to Submit If your qualifications, skills, and experience align with this position, we invite you to apply by submitting one PDF file that includes your resume, cover letter, and citizenship status, clearly outlining how your qualifications and experience make you a suitable candidate for the role. Please submit applications electronically in one file with the subject line “2026 -Labour Relations Specialist” by 4:30 p.m. November 11, 2026 to: hrapplications@brandonu.ca Please Note: Candidates may be required to successfully complete a technical skills test. This position is subject to a Criminal Record Check and Child Abuse Registry Check and the successful candidate will be responsible for fees incurred. We thank all applicants for their interest in this position, however, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted.  Short-listed candidates will be required to provide three (3) work-related references at the time of the interview. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. Should you require an accommodation during any phase of the recruitment process, contact HR at hr@brandonu.ca . All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/psac-sa-i-religion-faculty-of-arts/": {
      "title": "PSAC",
      "description": "PSAC – SA I – Religion, Faculty of Arts | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities PSAC – SA I – Religion, Faculty of Arts PSAC – SA I – Religion, Faculty of Arts Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on November 4, 2026. Classification: Student Assistant I Employee Group: PSAC Job Title: Equipment/Instrument Assistant Department: Religion, Faculty of Arts Wage or Salary: $17.15/hr Student Assistant I (SAI) Number of Hours to Work: 86.150: 2 positions x 5 hrs each; 86.202 2 positions x 4 hrs each Start Date: Nov. 5, 2026 Number of Positions available: 4 End Date of Employment: Dec. 10, 2026 Course title and number (if applicable): 86.150 and 86.202 Date Issued: October 29, 2026 Key Duties: Move equipment/instruments as required to locations on and off campus assist with assignment of equipment/instruments (operation of the computer (and some of its programs), as well as the sound equipment) other relevant duties as assigned 86.150 What is a Religion? -Up to a maximum of 5 hours for each of the two positions 86.202 Religion & Marginalization – Up to a maximum of 4 hours for each of the two positions Qualifications/Experience: Skillset: Little to no advanced skills or judgment Take direction, follow instruction and work under close supervision Ability to work independently and/or with others effectively Organized and detail oriented Education: Preference given to current Brandon University student, first year undergraduate is acceptable Experience: Previous experience an asset Familiarity with equipment/instruments, including proper use and maintenance To Apply: Please send your resume and cover letter as a single PDF document to Melissa Ballard at Arts@brandonu.ca with the course(s) you are applying to assist with indicated in the body of the email. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. Should you require an accommodation during any phase of the recruitment process, contact HR at hr@brandonu.ca . All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/2026-26-building-service-worker-i-full-time-physical-plant/": {
      "title": "2026",
      "description": "2026 – 26 – Building Service Worker I – Full-time, Physical Plant | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities 2026 – 26 – Building Service Worker I – Full-time,… 2026 – 26 – Building Service Worker I – Full-time, Physical Plant Application forms are available on the Brandon University website on Careers@BU . Completed applications, or resumés and cover letters are accepted by e-mail to hrapplications@brandonu.ca .  Please quote the Job Vacancy Number in the email subject line. Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on November 5, 2026 Job Vacancy Number: 2026 – 26 Employee Group: IUOE (D) Classification: Building Service Worker I (BSW I) Department: Physical Plant Type of Position: Full-Time, Regular Hours of Work: 36.25 hours per week Wage or Salary: $26.07 per hour Start Date: November 23, 2026 Probation or Trial Period: Three (3) months’ service Date Issued: October 29, 2026 Duties and Responsibilities: This position reports to the Director of Physical Plant and is responsible for a variety of tasks aimed at maintaining the cleanliness and upkeep of Brandon University. Duties include, but are not limited to cleaning, buffing and waxing floors, carpet care, auto scrubbing, changing lightbulbs, snow and ice removal, bed-making within university residences, cleaning washrooms, walls, and windows, garbage and recycling disposal, moving furniture, grounds maintenance, maintaining overall cleanliness of Brandon University as well as other relevant duties as assigned. Required Qualifications and Experience: The preferred candidate will possess a minimum of Grade 12 or GED, along with two (2) years of experience in institutional cleaning and groundskeeping, or a combination of equivalent education and experience. The candidate must be physically capable of performing all aspects of the role, including repetitive tasks such as bending, heavy lifting, pushing, pulling, and working in elevated areas using ladders. Experience using FAMIS 360 or other work-order software is an asset. A physical demands assessment will be conducted as part of the hiring process. The successful candidate must hold a valid Class 5 driver’s license and demonstrate the ability to work both independently and as part of a collaborative team. *NOTE* Candidates must be available and willing to work a variety of shifts, including early mornings, days, evenings and weekends with varying start times. Hours and location of work are subject to change based on operational needs. This position is subject to a Child Abuse Registry Check and Criminal Record Check.  The successful candidate will be responsible for any service charges incurred.  These checks must be submitted in accordance with the Policy in order to maintain employment. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. Should you require an accommodation during any phase of the recruitment process, contact HR at hr@brandonu.ca . All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    }
